From 9291e0bd1f03967609213629fa9cc7eff847e57c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zuiho <31877877+zuiho-kai@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:46:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] bothouse-iot: role dial, host push, mic uplink, touch keys on
 xiaozhi-esp32 v2.5.2

Squashed from the role-household firmware line (rh -> rh-uplink -> rh-dial-step2, up to
2026-10-31 "six capacitive conversation buttons" on Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-1.85C):

- keep the audio channel open so the host can push speech any time (CONFIG_RH_HOST_PUSH)
- no built-in local sounds, no on-board wake word by default
- stream the microphone to the host when idle (CONFIG_RH_ALWAYS_LISTEN)
- round role dial drawn with LVGL instead of the default xiaozhi face (CONFIG_RH_DIAL,
  spotpear sp-esp32-s3-1.28-box), using the cn_dial / cn_dial_lvgl components
- hello reports the screen profile; touch keys on the 1.85C board
- OTA URL is a placeholder, set at build time or via NVS
