+https://www.waveshare.net/shop/ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-1.85C.htm
+
+## Side copper electrodes (ESP-IDF 6)
+
+L1/L2/L3 use GPIO1/3/6; R1/R2/R3 use GPIO7/9/12. The existing BOOT
+button remains connected. Each electrode uses the same button component's
+single-click timing and debounce as BOOT, calling the same conversation action
+(start/interrupt; Wi-Fi provisioning while starting). No long-press or swipe
+callbacks are installed.
+
+The native `esp_driver_touch_sens` driver performs three initial scans and sets
+each electrode's threshold to 0.6% of its own baseline (minimum 1 count), with
+50% release hysteresis. The hardware filter maintains the baseline afterward.
+Keep fingers off the electrodes during initial calibration. The 0.6% ratio is a
+starting value, not a measured sensitivity guarantee through the 1.6 mm wall;
+confirm touch/no-touch readings on assembled hardware before shipping.
+
+Build from an exported IDF 6 environment:
+
+```sh
+python scripts/build.py waveshare/esp32-s3-touch-lcd-1.85c --name esp32-s3-touch-lcd-1.85c
+```
+
+The default build selects hardware v2.0. `config.json` enables task-watchdog panic
+and reboot; the SDK defaults enable both interrupt and idle-task watchdogs.
+These catch interrupt stalls and CPU starvation, not every application-level
+blocked wait. `partitions/v2/16m.csv` contains `otadata`, `ota_0`, and `ota_1`;
+`sdkconfig.defaults` enables bootloader rollback. Rollback only applies while a
+new image is pending verification (`Ota::MarkCurrentVersionValid` confirms it).
+
+Normal USB Serial/JTAG flashing can enter download mode automatically. It is
+not a replacement for physical recovery if firmware disables USB or changes
+its pins; retain access to the internal BOOT/RESET buttons for servicing.
+References: [Espressif USB Serial/JTAG guide](https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/stable/esp32s3/api-guides/usb-serial-jtag-console.html),
+[Waveshare board guide](https://www.waveshare.com/wiki/ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-1.85C).
